**What was wrong and is retracted.** Nothing numerical is retracted. Three corrections to how earlier lanes' numbers must be read, each measured here rather than argued. (1) btq201's 'POD-32/64/128 did NOT converge' is a STOPPING-RULE artefact. In this job every POD rank exits every one of its 900 time steps on the gradient rule with a worst per-step normalised gradient of 1.0e-06 or better and ZERO iteration-budget exits; the only quantity above tolerance is the INITIAL FIT's normalised gradient (4.5e-02 to 1.9e-01), whose relative residual is 9.1e-20 to 1.4e-17 — the POD initial fit is the square system R z = Q^T u_in, solved exactly, so ||J^T r||/(||J|| ||r||) is 0/0 and no iteration budget can move it. Nor would the error move: solved/best-found is 1.00000 to 1.00577, i.e. every POD solve already sits on its own projection floor. DESIGN.md section 5 pre-registered the rule that accepts an attained fit and reports btq201's stricter flag beside it; the report now argues this in prose with the numbers rather than leaving it to a flag column. (2) The head ablation's 'no POD rank up to k=128 (8K) matches the neural head' is true as measured but does NOT extend: at k'=256 and k'=512, ranks it never ran, POD overtakes the correction ladder on the evolved metric — POD-512 reaches 0.2184 % at 2929 ms against the dense q=256 rung's 0.5194 % at 4165 ms, better on BOTH axes, from a fully converged solve. On the all-times metric the certified-EQ ladder still owns the entire reduced frontier and no POD rank appears on it. (3) This lane's own DESIGN.md A3 retracts its first transfer design: qrg304's fixed-iterate reachable-state collector returns a FROZEN state whenever the first time step needs more iterations than it unrolls (29 at 64 intervals), which the smoke caught as sixteen IDENTICAL held-out rho values and a 1.1e-15 refit residual; transferred rules now collect the production dense query's own converged per-step states, and after the fix the same smoke certifies primary at both rungs with rho_max 0.097 and 0.060. That defect never touched job 1, which uses qrg304's rules unchanged at their own mesh. Also recorded: the free bank sits 1.538x above its STATIC projection floor (0.6027 % against 0.3918 %), which is a trajectory-vs-reconstruction difference, not solver slack.

