     1	"""3D rule selection from `c3desc*` escalation results (DESIGN 3.3 as amended by A1.7, A2.4, A2.5, A6.2, A6.3, A7.1).
     2	
     3	Per setting:
     4	  converged rule r_inf and the escalation statuses (from the job, where the rule was decided in-job);
     5	  for every ladder rule and both selection arms (fixed-sweep BE dt0 K=1; fixed-sweep LSPG-CN 2.5 dt0 K=2): A6.2
     6	  eligibility (saved by the job) and the worst distance to the r_inf run of the same arm, RECOMPUTED here independently
     7	  by decoding the coefficients through the bank at the 63^3 lattice coordinates (max over evolved times, relative to the
     8	  physical ||u0|| at the lattice);
     9	  m* per family (lattice: lat8192 ... lat131072; Gauss: gl24 ... gl48) = smallest rule with both arms eligible and worst
    10	  distance <= tau = 2.5e-4 on every case; the control lat256 must NOT qualify (else the selection is withheld:
    11	  non-discriminating);
    12	  deployed family = smaller sum of the two arms' median paired ratios in the family panels (A = r_inf fixed BE dt0; panels
    13	  must be valid); ties -> smaller m; fallbacks = the next two larger rungs of the deployed family, then 'unavailable'.
    14	A setting without a converged rule is 'unavailable' (no selection; the diagnostic-baseline ladder is reported only).
    15	Writes checks/SELECTION-3D.json (or --out). Smoke inputs are refused unless --allow-smoke.
